# Secret of Bloodbending countered by Counterspell (paid for with Black Lotus): the spell never resolves, so no control is created at all,
# not for the combat phase and not for the turn: on turn 4 Bot2 makes its own decisions throughout its combat phase, nothing waits for it
# (NextTurnControlledBy), and the card is in the graveyard (CR 701.6a), not exiled: "Exile Secret of Bloodbending" is part of its resolution.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Secret of Bloodbending
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Counterspell
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Secret of Bloodbending.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot2.Hand.Counterspell.Cast(Stack.Secret of Bloodbending)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard = Secret of Bloodbending; Black Lotus
? Exile =
? Bot2.NextTurnControlledBy = (absent)
[T4 Bot2.BeginCombat]
? Bot2.ControlledBy = (absent)

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Secret of Bloodbending; Black Lotus
Bot2.Graveyard = Counterspell; Black Lotus
